<main id="main" class="container">
  <%- include('../partials/flash') %>

  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="lead">Plain English. If anything here is unclear, tell the IT office
  and we will rewrite it.</p>

  <h2>What WhereITis is for</h2>
  <p>WhereITis helps students, staff, and the custodian office reunite lost items
  with their owners on the CSPC campus. It is a coordination tool — not a
  guarantee.</p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It is not a replacement for the Registrar's office or the Student Affairs
    office for any official purpose.</li>
    <li>It does not guarantee that any item will be recovered.</li>
    <li>It does not handle payment, fines, or fees of any kind.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Report only items you actually lost or actually found.</li>
    <li>Do not file a claim you know is false. Claims are reviewed by staff, and
    false claims are referred to Student Affairs.</li>
    <li>Do not use the system to stalk, harass, or track another person.</li>
    <li>Do not scrape, automate, or bulk-request pages.</li>
    <li>Do not upload or link to content that is illegal, hateful, or not yours
    to share.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Consequences of abuse</h2>
  <p>Depending on severity: the claim may be rejected, the account may be
  suspended, and — for the most serious cases — the matter is referred to the
  Student Affairs office for disciplinary action under existing college rules.</p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>WhereITis is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. The college does
  not accept liability for lost items, missed matches, or claims decided
  incorrectly. Staff decisions are made in good faith on the information provided.</p>

  <h2>Handling disputes</h2>
  <p>If you disagree with a claim decision, contact the Student Affairs office.
  The college's existing grievance procedure applies.</p>

  <h2>Source code</h2>
  <p>WhereITis is open source under the MIT licence. The repository is linked from
  the project's GitHub page and included in the midterm submission.</p>
</main>

